{"id":"systemd-user-sessions.service.8","n":"systemd-user-sessions.service","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"systemd","ver":"252-51.el9_6.3.rocky.0.1","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/s/systemd-252-51.el9_6.3.rocky.0.1.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/systemd-user-sessions.service.8.gz","sha256":"18efce8a1047fba67a23f2d47ff8d15332fe0ecafc2571dcdc235d6731ff2297","date":"","origin":"systemd 252"},"u":{"pkg":"systemd","ver":"249.11-0ubuntu3.23","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/s/systemd/systemd_249.11-0ubuntu3.23_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/systemd-user-sessions.service.8.gz","sha256":"537d9b1e23b0cb6ae3d2034b0342384b832d3ef92b585feba59b3b9e8bb2f957","date":"","origin":"systemd 249"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"Permit user logins after boot, prohibit user logins at shutdown","same":false,"r":[["NAME","<p>systemd-user-sessions.service, systemd-user-sessions - Permit user logins after boot, prohibit user logins at shutdown</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p>systemd-user-sessions.service</p> <p>/usr/lib/systemd/systemd-user-sessions</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>systemd-user-sessions.service is a service that controls user logins through <b>pam_nologin</b>(8). After basic system initialization is complete, it removes /run/nologin, thus permitting logins. Before system shutdown, it creates /run/nologin, thus prohibiting further logins.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>systemd</b>(1), <b>systemd-logind.service</b>(8), <b>pam_nologin</b>(8)</p>"]],"u":[["NAME",0],["SYNOPSIS","<p>systemd-user-sessions.service</p> <p>/lib/systemd/systemd-user-sessions</p>"],["DESCRIPTION",2],["SEE ALSO",3]],"diff":{"r":[],"u":[]}}